      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC during these lines at least PidChange DELETE/CREATE events are generated, and followed by the BluetoothStopped/Started events.\n\nI guess this may break the state machine one day if someone added something to action_on_bluetooth_stopped while not being aware of the adapter may have been started by this function.\n\nNot sure if it\u0027s good enough but I think we may add a new ProcessState::Restarting state, and handle the restart in `action_on_bluetooth_stopped`. That is, the state change is\n```\nRestartBluetooth -\u003e action_restart_bluetooth: set Restarting, run process_manager.stop\nBluetoothStopped -\u003e action_on_bluetooth_stopped: set TurningOn, run process_manager.start\nBluetoothStarted -\u003e action_on_bluetooth_started: set On\n```\nWDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1345,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1348,
        "endChar": 94
